-- title:
--   Ordinarity at p of a Hecke–Galois datum from residual ordinarity
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p \ne 2$, a positive integer $N$ with $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$, and a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, of characteristic zero, with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal, let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $T$ be a noetherian local ring, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, which is a finite free $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with local structure map. Let $H$ be a Hecke–Galois datum for these data: a homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ reducing to $\theta$, with $\mathcal{O}[\mathrm{im}\,\pi] = T$, surjective residue map from $\mathcal{O}$, the lifting property that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued character reducing to $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ via an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T \to \mathcal{O}$, together with a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomial at each prime $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ is $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$, and whose residual representation $\mathrm{ResidueField}(T) \otimes_T \rho.V$ is absolutely irreducible. Assume that this residual representation, regarded as a two-dimensional representation with coefficients in the field $\mathrm{ResidueField}(T)$, is ordinary at $p$. The conclusion is that $\rho$ itself is ordinary at $p$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit in $P$ there is a $T$-submodule $L \subseteq \rho.V$ spanned by the first vector of some basis indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2$, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, and such that $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $v$ and all $\sigma$ in the image of the inertia subgroup of $P$.
--
--   This is the transport of the ordinarity condition from the residual representation to the $\lambda$-adic Hecke–Galois representation, in the shape used when the residue characteristic $p$ exactly divides the level. It is invoked when the local conditions of a Hecke–Galois datum are assembled, in particular in the construction of data satisfying prescribed ordinary or flat conditions feeding the patching argument.
